n and  they just think as you say on your note  there  uh no one to talk to unremitted silence  24 hours a day  unbearable torture well it  my advice is to do what i've done but  not not necessarily in the same way  you've got to somehow go  out and meet people which i found almost  impossible under the  threat of this virus but i determined to  do it  because it was almost killing me sitting  here  in my little room where the phone is  ringing now  and having nobody to talk to the phone  never rang then  but by goodness me it's certainly  ringing now  would you like some good news of course  you would lockdown has seen many special  events including weddings called  off but it's also shown us that love  knows no limits one couple who have kept  an ocean apart by coronavirus  restrictions finally managed to tie the  knot  in scotland priya and sandy had  originally planned to say  i do in malaysia but travel restrictions  brought in  in march have made that impossible and  after months of trying to find an  alternative plan the couple would give  them the go-ahead  to exchange vows in sterling in scotland  and the newlywed couple  join me now from kentucky great to see  you both  and congratulations great news um why  don't we start  priya right at the beginning tell me how  you met because it was quite unusual  i was just trying to kill time in the  heathrow airport and  i opened up this app that i'd heard  about on my trip  from another colleague he said it was  called dill mill  and it's uh just a dating app for south  asian specifically  and i thought oh well you know what the  heck what do i have to lose so  i uh logged onto the app and it's  very neat you've got all sorts of  filters you can filter by height  you can filter by by religion and  whatnot  and you know you can also filter by  location  so i just opened up all my filters and i  only had about a 20 or 30 minute layover  but in that 20 or 30  faded minutes i i happened to  see this beautiful face pop